Some parsing rules and finding ideas come from codeburn (MIT, AgentSeal),
github.com/getagentseal/codeburn v0.9.27, rewritten in Rust. Rules ported:
- parser.ts: streaming dedup (last usage, first timestamp per message id), global message-id dedup
  across resumed and forked sessions, recursive subagent file discovery, human prompt filters
- context-tree.ts: compaction boundary metadata
- models.ts calculateCost: the cost formula only (no price table, no price fetching)
- bash-utils.ts: shell command splitting and prefix stripping
- optimize.ts: re-read and MCP coverage finding ideas

Provider formats taken from codeburn v0.9.27 (commit 7ecc87f), rewritten in Rust:
- providers/antigravity.ts and docs/providers/antigravity.md: gen_metadata / steps protobuf field numbers,
  placeholder model table, tool names (crates/core/src/providers/agy)
- providers/codex.ts and docs/providers/codex.md: rollout records, token_count delta and fork dedup key, tool
  names (crates/core/src/providers/codex)
- providers/opencode-file-parser.ts, sqlite-session-parser.ts and docs/providers/opencode.md: JSON storage and
  SQLite layouts (crates/core/src/providers/opencode)

No code, price data, network code or presentation is copied.

