The default CO2 method is a port of EcoLogits 0.11.3 (MPL-2.0, GenAI Impact), github.com/mlco2/ecologits,
commit d586c3566da37ecd2c35878d77ae6e7de1a0719c (2026-10-23):
- crates/co2-data/src/ecologits/models.json: ecologits/data/models.json, unmodified.
- crates/co2-data/src/ecologits/mod.rs: Rust port of ecologits/impacts/llm.py (formula and constants),
  ecologits/tracers/utils.py (provider PUE, WUE and zone) and the US and Swedish grid GWP and WUE values of
  ecologits/data/electricity_mixes.json. Changes: GWP, energy and water only; no time to first token and no measured
  latency, so impacts are per output token; the user may replace the grid intensity.
These two files are covered by the Mozilla Public License 2.0 (text in crates/co2-data/src/ecologits/LICENSE,
also https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/); their source form is the files themselves, shipped with tokenwhy's source.
The rest of tokenwhy is not covered by MPL-2.0.
Tests check the port against the spec vectors of EcoLogits.js (MPL-2.0), github.com/mlco2/ecologits.js,
spec 0.2.0 (read 2026-10-23); no code is copied from it.

